<h1><span lang="EN-US">Select Boundaries</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="whs4"><span lang="EN-US"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">This command is accessible from</font></span> <b><i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select &gt; Scan Data &gt; Boundaries</b></span></i></b> <span lang="EN-US">(for scan data) and</span> <b><i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select &gt; Mesh &gt; Boundaries</b></span></i></b> <span lang="EN-US">or by pressing</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + Shift + Alt + B</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">(for meshes).</span></p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Select Boundaries</span> <span lang="EN-US">command selects boundary triangles of visible scans and meshes. Boundary triangles are those triangles, which edges and/or points belong to the boundaries (inner and outer) of the entity.</span></p>
<p class="whs4"><span lang="EN-US"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">This command works on scan data and meshes only. Note that it removes any previous scan data and mesh selections. Selections of other data types remain unaffected.</font></span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path">Select &gt; Scan Data &gt; Boundaries</span></i> <span lang="EN-US">command is grayed if there are no scan data or all scans are hidden.</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path">Select &gt; Mesh &gt; Boundaries</span></i> <span lang="EN-US">command is grayed if there are no meshes or all meshes are hidden.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for Mesh</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP225895654" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/image19.gif" width="650px" height="417px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p>Selected triangles on a mesh boundary</p>
</div>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for Scan Data</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP938018232" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/image20.gif" width="600px" height="429px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
<p>Selected triangles on scan data boundaries</p>
</div>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-US">: When applying this command on scan data, boundaries of every patch will be selected. This is not valid only when the entity is scanned with area sampling after scan  in this case the whole scan consists of a single patch.</span></p>
